          "cuecs": [
            {
              "text": "User entities are responsible for understanding and complying with their contractual obligations to Meridian. (ISMS-14)",
              "criteria": [
                "CC1.3",
                "CC2.1",
                "CC2.3",
                "CC9.2",
                "C1.1",
                "PI1.1"
              ],
              "controlCodes": [
                "ISMS-14"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "User Entities are responsible to share the IP(s) that need to be whitelisted to gain access to their CSP production workspace instance on a timely basis. (CSC-01)",
              "criteria": [
                "CC6.6",
                "CC6.7"
              ],
              "controlCodes": [
                "CSC-01"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "User Entities are responsible to nominate appropriate personnel to receive the administrator credentials to their CSP workspace. / User Entities are responsible for access creation, modification, revocation, reconciliation, and review of users and their privileges within their CSP workspace. / User Entities are responsible for enabling SSO or OTP for MFA during login to their CSP workspace.",
              "criteria": [
                "CC6.1",
                "CC6.2",
                "CC6.3",
                "CC6.8",
                "PI1.5"
              ],
              "controlCodes": []
            },
            {
              "text": "User Entities are responsible for the security, encryption, and access policies of the source data lakes (e.g. Snowflake) that they connect to the CSP workspace. / User Entities are responsible for managing network security controls within their environment.",
              "criteria": [
                "CC6.1",
                "CC6.6",
                "CC6.7"
              ],
              "controlCodes": []
            },
            {
              "text": "User Entities are responsible to opt-in to be notified about the real-time response and availability metrics of CSP on the status webpage. (CSC-21)",
              "criteria": [
                "A1.2"
              ],
              "controlCodes": [
                "CSC-21"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "User Entities are responsible to periodically review the support website containing resources such as product documentation, best practices, training materials, guides, troubleshooting tips, and community forums to effectively utilize CSP. (CSC-22)",
              "criteria": [
                "PI1.1",
                "PI1.2"
              ],
              "controlCodes": [
                "CSC-22"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "User Entities are responsible for timely communication of their repatriation.",
              "criteria": [
                "CC6.5",
                "C1.1",
                "C1.2"
              ],
              "controlCodes": []
            },
            {
              "text": "User Entities are responsible for timely communication of incidents, breaches, requests, and / or issues within their CSP workspace. / User Entities are responsible for timely communication of confirmation of closure upon resolution of their issue(s) and / or request(s) (CUS-02)",
              "criteria": [
                "CC7.1",
                "CC7.2",
                "CC7.3",
                "CC7.4",
                "CC7.5"
              ],
              "controlCodes": [
                "CUS-02"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "csocs": [
            {
              "text": "Customer data communicated through AWS service interfaces is encrypted during transmission over external networks. / Internal communication between key AWS components where customer data is transmitted / involved is secured using SSL or equivalent mechanism(s). / Access privileges are reviewed periodically to determine if access rights are commensurate to the user’s job duties. Access is modified based on the results of the reviews. / Administrative access to the service environment is controlled through defined interfaces that require authentication using appropriate credentials. Privileges (i.e., read, write) are restricted to authorized personnel through designated channels based on job responsibilities. / Procedures have been established for granting temporary access for AWS personnel to customer data and applications upon appropriate approval for customer support or incident handling purposes. / User groups and Access Control Lists have been stablished to restrict access to network devices in the scope boundary. / Customer credentials used to access AWS services meet the applicable password policy requirements. / Customer data that is designated as “confidential” is protected while in storage within AWS services. / Logical segregation is implemented to restrict unauthorized access to other customer tenants. / Customer data that is designated as confidential is protected while in storage within AWS services. / Data at rest is encrypted using AES 256-bit encryption, which is provided by KMS of AWS. / Access to network devices in the scope boundary is restricted through a limited number of entry points that require authentication over an encrypted connection. / The network is segregated to separate customer traffic from management traffic. A monitoring system has been implemented to monitor the AWS platforms for potential malicious activity and intrusion past service trust boundaries.",
              "criteria": [
                "CC6.1",
                "CC6.2",
                "CC6.3"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Procedures have been established to restrict physical access to the server room to authorized users, vendors, contractors, and visitors. / Physical access to the server room is reviewed quarterly and verified by the server room Management team. / Physical access mechanisms (e.g., access card readers, biometric devices, man traps/portals, cages, locked cabinets) have been implemented and are administered to restrict access to authorized individuals. / Amazon Web Services, Inc. is responsible for managing physical security of the AWS platform.",
              "criteria": [
                "CC6.4"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Environmental controls such as fire extinguishers, smoke detectors, UPS, etc. exists within the premises and Data Center. / Vendor conducts the preventive maintenance of this equipment on a periodic basis. / A Business Continuity and Disaster Recovery (BC / DR) Standard Operating Procedure is developed, and documentation includes the defined information security and availability requirements. / The BCP team conducts testing of the business continuity and disaster recovery plans established for AWS services, per the defined testing schedule for different loss scenario. Each loss scenario is tested at least annually. Issues identified during testing are resolved and plans are updated accordingly. / AWS management reviews portal performance monthly to evaluate compliance with customer SLA requirements. / Backups of key AWS service components and secrets are performed regularly and stored in fault tolerant (isolated) facilities. / Critical AWS components have been designed with redundancy to sustain isolated faults and minimize disruptions to customer services. / Customer data is automatically replicated within AWS to minimize isolated faults. / Backup restoration procedures are defined, and backup data integrity checks are performed through standard restoration activities. / Data centre Management team maintains data center-managed environmental equipment within the facility according to documented policy and maintenance procedures.",
              "criteria": [
                "A1.1",
                "A1.2",
                "A1.3"
              ]
            }
          ],
